    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d274">

                <pb facs="0376" n="296" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg296"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Signor
                            Carignani.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-08-12"><hi rendition="#italic">August 12,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 700.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 30th ultimo, giving certain information obtained by the
                    Italian consular authorities relating to the killing of two Italians and the
                    wounding of a third at Erwin, Miss.</p>
                <p>This information has been communicated to the governor of Mississippi.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
